{
  "description": "CSV export/import in Strong's column layout. Weights are kg in the model; the CSV holds them in a unit (the 'Weight Unit' column, a unit in the Weight header like 'Weight (lbs)', or the default unit). Set Order is W/D/F for warm-up/drop/failure sets, else the number of the normal set. Zero weight, reps, distance or seconds import as empty. Durations export as '1h 5m' or '45m'. Compare weights with tolerance 0.01. Newer Strong exports may use ';' between fields (and ',' as the decimal mark), units in the Duration and Distance headers ('Duration (sec)', 'Distance (km)'), ISO dates, and rows that are not sets ('Rest Timer'), which are skipped.",
  "fields": [
    {
      "fields": [
        "a",
        "b,c",
        "d\"e",
        "f\ng",
        ""
      ],
      "text": "a,\"b,c\",\"d\"\"e\",\"f\ng\","
    }
  ],
